IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-55. NOUNS of a cross-reference. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Planning and Building Law, 5725-1965, or of its regulations. It records five citations whose numbers do not point at what their words describe,
-- two second readings of two of them, and three citations that are sound and stand beside them as controls. For each citation it types what the citing words say they point at,
-- what the target is, and where each of the two readings comes from. A citation whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- Two kinds say, in their own words, that the consolidation does not print what the citing words need; one kind says that the wording of a repealed section was not read.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the deposited consolidation text, with whole-page line numbers, and a tag where the source is not the Law;
-- `ext:[SH ...]` and `ext:[KT ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `a provision of section 145 under which an application becomes absorbed`
    `a paragraph (4) of subsection (א2) of section 145, which the consolidation does not print: it prints that subsection as one sentence with no paragraphs`
    `the Minister's setting of the preconditions for absorbing an application`
    `the treating of an application as absorbed when the engineer gives no notice within the Minister's period, which is what paragraph (4) of subsection (א3) of section 145 prints`
    `the objection a holder of a right in the land may file against a short-route application, subsection (א2) of section 152`
    `a section of the Law under which inspectors are authorised, whose wording this row did not read`
    `a section of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text`
    `section 145א of the Law, the section on the consent of the Israel Land Authority to a permit application`
    `a definition of the respondent in a section 198א of the Law`
    `no section 198א of the Law: the consolidation prints no section with that number`
    `the definition of the respondent in subsection (א) of section 198 of the Law`
    `the list of arbitrator appraisers, section 202ג of the Law`
    `the conditions of qualification to serve as an arbitrator appraiser, in a paragraph (2) of a subsection (ה) of section 202`
    `section 202 of the Law, one paragraph on compensation for the stopping of an exceeding use, with no subsections`
    `paragraph (2) of section 202ה of the Law, a condition of qualification to serve as an arbitrator appraiser`

-- Five kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for a limb (a) whose repeal and commencement were read from the official pages while that nothing later brought the section back rests on the consolidation.
-- The third kind is the honest name for a limb (b) whose words were read from a page image of the official instrument that published them while that no later instrument touched them rests on the consolidation.
-- The fifth kind is for a second reading that I supplied and that no page prints.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the same words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the official page image of the words as published; that no later instrument touched them is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`
    `a reading supplied by this row; no page prints it`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
